00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.210
Beyond.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.210
Thanks for picking me.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.840
Thank you.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:19.180
I was wondering with all the talk about polling
that we always hear.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.439
This might be a dumb question, but where do
people get polled to collect this info?

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:29.230
Speaker 1: You look at the methodology of
each poll and it will tell you that and it

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.370
will tell you the combination.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:34.050
You know, typically it's landlines, cell phones.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.750
Sometimes there are online elements to the
poll, but there's not one answer to that,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.750
and it's in the methodology.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.330
Speaker 2: Okay.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:47.260
Because I was thinking, you know, if people
are getting reached out to on landlines and

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:53.511
phones and I don't know, most people at this
point don't pick up four calls that are, you

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:55.149
know, suspicious or they don't recognize.

00:00:55.149 --> 00:00:57.730
Then I don't know.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.800
How much stock can you put into polling in
that case?

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.460
Speaker 1: Yeah, your skepticism isn't new.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:07.670
This is an issue that people have talked about
for a while, which is especially if it's only

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:08.740
landlines.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:14.409
Most polls are not only landlines at this
point in time, I think the bigger and more

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:23.040
accurate concern around polling is only certain
people are even going to entertain a call

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.040
from pollsters.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:28.380
I mean, listen, I'm I'm so busy, for example,
I don't really talk on the phone.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.299
I don't even use my I barely use my phone.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:34.670
I have periods of time where 4 hours I'm just
away from my phone.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:36.040
I rarely pick it up.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.610
I don't often I don't even listen to voicemails.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.580
I'm basically like conducting business via
email for most of the things that I have going

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.580
on.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:49.810
So it's true that there are only some people
who are even willing to get on the phone with

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.020
a pollster.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:56.420
The way pollsters deal with that is they adjust
their sample to account for that.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:01.110
But it's a fair question to say to what degree
can they really accurately and fairly adjust

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.110
the sample?

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:03.439
I think it's fair.

00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:08.920
Polling has, by and large, still been pretty
accurate in most cases over the last four

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.959
years, although we certainly saw some specific
instances in which it was not.

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:15.560
So all good questions and important things
to ask.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.700
Speaker 2: All right.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.700
